    "notes": "Native PMTiles footprints position forty palace and garden structures. Clearance probes pass through the modeled gates at every level. Only the named bridge trace is replaced. Exterior reconstruction of the mapped palace courts and principal Secret Garden pavilions and Geumcheongyo’s paired stone arches. Building elevations use six-meter standard terrain samples. Individual dancheong motifs, roof figures and carved plaques are interpreted at viewer scale. Interiors, isolated service buildings and the far northern Jade Stream are outside this reconstruction. The bridge follows the mapped footpath. Native terrain stays in place, so channel detail below the arch openings depends on terrain resolution."
  },
